                <pb facs="0359" n="271" sameAs="frus:frus1892/pg271"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Sir Julian Pauncefote to Mr. Blaine.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >British Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1892-02-29"><hi rendition="#italic">February 29, 1892</hi></date>.
                        (Received March 2.)</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to my note of the 25th November
                    last, and to your note of the 30th of the same month on the subject of the
                    charge of immigrants who are not permitted to land at Boston, I have the honor
                    to recall the matter to your attention and to express the hope that I may be
                    favored with a reply to my above-mentioned note at an early date.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Julian
                    Pauncefote.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
